---
import MotionPage from '@/components/MotionPage.astro';
import ForFramework from '@/components/ForFramework.astro';
import ApiName from '@/components/ApiName.astro';
import Code from '@/components/Code.astro';
import MotionStage from '@/components/motion/MotionStage.astro';
import MotionUsage from '@/components/motion/MotionUsage.astro';
import MotionOptions from '@/components/motion/MotionOptions.astro';
import MotionTokens from '@/components/motion/MotionTokens.astro';
import Inbox from '@/components/motion/scenes/Inbox.astro';
import { InboxControls } from '@/components/motion/scenes/InboxControls';
import { MotionListReact } from '@/examples/react/motion-list.tsx';
import { MotionListAngular } from '@/examples/angular/motion-list.ts';
import MotionListSvelte from '@/examples/svelte/motion-list.svelte';
import { chipClass } from '@/components/motionDemo';

const defineListItem = `import { defineMotion } from '@udixio/motion';

// Items that enter together start one step apart, from the first one. A leaving item is taken out of the flow,
// so the items around it close the gap while it fades.
defineMotion('list-item', {
  verb: 'appear',
  keyframes: [{ opacity: 0, y: 16 }, { opacity: 1, y: 0 }],
  stagger: 'normal',
  origin: 'first',
  exit: 'out-of-flow',
});`;
---
<MotionPage
  slug="lists"
  title="Motion: make a list appear"
  description="Items added together cascade in visual order; a leaving item lets its neighbours close the gap. In HTML, React, Angular and Svelte."
  frameworkSwitch
>
  <ForFramework as="span" slot="summary">
    <Fragment slot="html">Put <code>data-motion="cascade reflow"</code> on each item: items added together cascade in, and a leaving item lets its neighbours close the gap.</Fragment>
    <Fragment slot="react">Render each item as a <code>&lt;Motion as="li" name="cascade reflow"&gt;</code> inside a <code>&lt;Presence&gt;</code>: items added together cascade in, and a leaving item lets its neighbours close the gap.</Fragment>
    <Fragment slot="angular">Put <code>udxMotion="cascade reflow"</code> on each item of an <code>&#64;for</code>: items added together cascade in, and a leaving item lets its neighbours close the gap.</Fragment>
    <Fragment slot="svelte">Attach <code>motion('cascade reflow')</code> and <code>transition:presence</code> to each item of an <code>&#123;#each&#125;</code> block: items added together cascade in, and a leaving item lets its neighbours close the gap.</Fragment>
  </ForFramework>

  <MotionStage scene="inbox" label="Live example: Make a list appear" height={384}>
    <Fragment slot="controls"><InboxControls client:visible size="page" /></Fragment>
    <Inbox />
    <Fragment slot="readout"><span class={`${chipClass} tracking-normal`} data-inbox-readout>origin: 'first' · stagger: 'normal' · exit: 'out-of-flow'</span></Fragment>
  </MotionStage>

  <h2>Make the items of a list enter and leave</h2>
  <p>
    Give each item two motions: a presence, which makes it enter and leave, and <code>reflow</code>, which makes it follow
    its neighbours. The preset <code>cascade</code> is a presence with <code>stagger: 'normal'</code>.
  </p>
  <ForFramework>
    <Fragment slot="html">
      <p>Put <code>data-motion="cascade reflow"</code> on each item of the list, and call <code>connectMotion()</code> once for the page. Then:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Insert several items in one task: they cascade in, in visual order.</li>
        <li>Set <code>hidden</code> on an item to remove it: its exit plays, then it is hidden and the others close the gap.</li>
        <li>Do not remove an item from the DOM to make it leave: it goes at once, with no exit.</li>
      </ul>
    </Fragment>
    <Fragment slot="react">
      <p>Render each item as a <code>&lt;Motion as="li" name="cascade reflow"&gt;</code> with a <code>key</code>, inside one <code>&lt;Presence&gt;</code> around the list. Then:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Add several items in one render: they cascade in, in visual order.</li>
        <li>Remove an item from your state: <code>&lt;Presence&gt;</code> keeps it on the page until its exit has played, then removes it.</li>
      </ul>
    </Fragment>
    <Fragment slot="angular">
      <p>Add <code>Motion</code> to your component's <code>imports</code>, and put <code>udxMotion="cascade reflow"</code> on each item of an <code>&#64;for</code> loop, tracked by an id. Then:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Add several items in one change: they cascade in, in visual order.</li>
        <li>Remove an item from your list: Angular keeps it on the page until its exit has played, then removes it.</li>
      </ul>
    </Fragment>
    <Fragment slot="svelte">
      <p>Attach <code>motion('cascade reflow')</code> and <code>transition:presence</code> to each item of an <code>&#123;#each&#125;</code> block, keyed by an id. Then:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Add several items in one update: they cascade in, in visual order.</li>
        <li>Remove an item from your array: <code>presence</code> keeps it until its exit has played, then Svelte removes it.</li>
      </ul>
    </Fragment>
  </ForFramework>
  <MotionUsage name="motion-lists-markup" live={false} />

  <h2>Add and dismiss messages</h2>
  <ForFramework>
    <p slot="html">The HTML code adds three messages at the top. A message that you swipe away, or focus and delete, flies out, and then the list lets it go.</p>
    <p slot="react">The example adds three messages at the top, keeps five at most, and dismisses a message with its button. A dismissed message plays its exit before the list lets it go.</p>
    <p slot="angular">The example adds three messages at the top, keeps five at most, and dismisses a message with its button. A dismissed message plays its exit before the list lets it go.</p>
    <p slot="svelte">The example adds three messages at the top, keeps five at most, and dismisses a message with its button. A dismissed message plays its exit before the list lets it go.</p>
  </ForFramework>
  <MotionUsage name="motion-list" previewHeight={[520, 704]}>
    <MotionListReact slot="react" client:visible />
    <MotionListAngular slot="angular" client:visible />
    <MotionListSvelte slot="svelte" client:visible />
  </MotionUsage>

  <h2>Set the stagger and the exit</h2>
  <p>
    Define your own list item with <code>defineMotion()</code> when the cascade or the exit must differ from the preset.
    Its <code>stagger</code> sets the step between the items that enter together: <code>tight</code> (20 ms),
    <code>normal</code> (50 ms) or <code>loose</code> (100 ms). The steps are capped at 400 ms in all.
  </p>
  <p>
    <code>origin</code> sets where the cascade starts: <code>first</code>, the default, <code>last</code>, or
    <code>center</code>, which starts in the middle and spreads both ways.
  </p>
  <p>
    <code>exit</code> sets how a leaving item moves its neighbours. <code>in-place</code>, the default, keeps the item where
    it is until its exit has played. <code>out-of-flow</code> takes it out of the flow when the exit starts, so the items
    around it close the gap while it fades.
  </p>
  <Code data-code={defineListItem} data-language="ts" />
  <p>
    Then give each item the name of your motion, in place of <code>cascade</code>:
    <ApiName html={'data-motion="list-item reflow"'} react={'name="list-item reflow"'} angular={'udxMotion="list-item reflow"'} svelte="motion('list-item reflow')" />.
  </p>

  <h2>Options</h2>
  <p>These options apply to a list item defined with the verb <code>appear</code>. <code>split</code> cuts text, so it is left out here.</p>
  <MotionOptions verb="appear" omit={['split']} />

  <h2>Timing and tokens</h2>
  <p>
    A new item moves in on the default spatial spring, and fades in on the default effects spring. A leaving item plays its
    exit on the default effects spring, and its neighbours follow it on the default spatial spring. The steps of the cascade
    come from the stagger token.
  </p>
  <MotionTokens tokens={['spring.default.spatial', 'spring.default.effects', 'stagger.normal']} />

  <h2>Reduced motion</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>A new item is a short fade, and the items that enter together fade in together: the cascade has no delays.</li>
    <li>A leaving item fades in place, whatever <code>exit</code> says: it does not leave the flow.</li>
    <li>Set <code>--udx-motion: none</code> on the list to show the end state at once.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Limits</h2>
  <ul>
    <ForFramework as="li">
      <Fragment slot="html">If you remove an item from the DOM, it goes at once, with no exit: set <code>hidden</code> instead.</Fragment>
      <Fragment slot="react">If you stop rendering the <code>&lt;Presence&gt;</code> itself, its items go at once, with no exit: keep it rendered, and put the condition inside it.</Fragment>
      <Fragment slot="angular">If an item is a child component, Angular does not wait for its exit when it removes the child: put <code>udxMotion</code> on the child's host element, in the parent's template.</Fragment>
      <Fragment slot="svelte">If a parent block removes the item, Svelte plays no transition: put <code>transition:presence</code> on the element that its own <code>&#123;#each&#125;</code> block adds and removes.</Fragment>
    </ForFramework>
    <li>If more than eight items enter together at <code>normal</code>, the ninth and the later ones start together, 400 ms after the first: the cascade is capped at 400 ms.</li>
    <li>If you use <code>exit: 'out-of-flow'</code> on a list that is not positioned, the leaving item is placed against an ancestor that is: add <code>relative</code> to the list.</li>
  </ul>
</MotionPage>
